      "problem": "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-z+2?$",
      "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-z+2 & =c \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2-c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we let $2-c=C,$ we get a family of hyperbolic paraboloids:\n\n$$\nz={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+C,\\,c\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$",
